Create a single-file HTML calorie intake tracker app with no backend, 
no build steps, and no external dependencies except Chart.js from CDN.

## Design
- Green health-themed color scheme with gradient accents
- CSS custom properties for light and dark mode (toggle stored in localStorage)
- Sticky header with app title and dark/light mode toggle
- Two-column layout: 270px sidebar on the left, main content on the right
- Fully responsive — stacks to single column on mobile
- Smooth transitions on theme change

## User Profile (Sidebar)
- Input fields: Name, Gender (Male/Female), Age, Weight (kg), Height (cm), 
  Activity Level (Sedentary / Lightly Active / Moderately Active / Very Active)
- Calculate daily calorie goal using the Mifflin-St Jeor BMR formula:
  Male:   BMR = (10 × weight) + (6.25 × height) − (5 × age) + 5
  Female: BMR = (10 × weight) + (6.25 × height) − (5 × age) − 161
  Multiply BMR by activity multiplier: 1.2 / 1.375 / 1.55 / 1.725
- Save profile to localStorage and restore on page load

## Food Entry
- Search input with autocomplete against a built-in database of 88+ common foods
- Foods have: name, calories per 100g, category, default unit, 
  and macros (carbs, protein, fat per 100g)
- Categories: Fruits, Vegetables, Grains, Protein, Dairy, Snacks, Beverages
- Quantity field with unit selector: Piece / Bowl / Cup / Gram / ml
- Convert units to grams to calculate actual calories and macros
- If food is not in the database, show a manual calorie entry fallback
- Add food button appends entry to today's log

## Dashboard (Main Area)
- Circular SVG progress ring showing calories consumed vs daily goal
  - Ring color shifts: green → orange → red as you approach/exceed goal
  - Displays consumed calories in center, label below
- 4 KPI tiles in a grid: Calories Consumed, Calories Remaining, Daily Goal, Items Logged
- Macro progress bars for Carbs, Protein, Fat 
  (normalized against recommended daily targets: 300g carbs, 50g protein, 65g fat)
- Doughnut chart showing calorie distribution by food category
- Bar chart showing calories per individual food entry
- Both charts use Chart.js 4.4 from CDN

## Nutrition Guide Panel (Collapsible Sidebar Section)
- Recommended daily calorie ranges by gender and age group
- Macronutrient split guidelines (Carbs 45–65%, Protein 10–35%, Fat 20–35%)
- Micronutrient highlights: fiber, water, sugar, sodium
- Dynamic tip that updates based on current intake 
  (under goal / near goal / over goal)

## Food Log Table
- Columns: Food | Category | Quantity | Unit | Calories | Time | Remove button
- Color-coded category badges
- Scrollable with totals row at the bottom
- "Clear Today" button to reset all entries

## Persistence
- Save today's food log to localStorage
- Restore entries on page load
- Profile settings also persisted

## Tech stack
- HTML5, CSS3 with custom properties
- Vanilla JavaScript ES6+ only
- Chart.js 4.4 via CDN (jsdelivr)
- No frameworks, no build tools, no npm
